            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/agents.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TriageFlow — AI Agent Configuration\n2: \n3: > Master agent guide for TriageFlow: AI-assisted patient triage showcase built with Symfony 7.4 + React + symfony/ai. This file governs how AI agents (OpenCode + Subagents) operate across the entire project.\n4: \n5: ## Quick Reference\n6: \n7: ```bash\n8: # Start backend dev server\n9: cd backend && symfony server:start\n10: \n11: # Start frontend dev server\n12: cd frontend && npm run dev\n13: \n14: # Run backend tests\n15: cd backend && php bin/phpunit\n16: \n17: # Run frontend tests\n18: cd frontend && npm run test\n19: \n20: # Generate synthetic case (manual trigger)\n21: cd backend && php bin/console app:synthetic-case:generate\n22: \n23: # Run scheduler (auto-generate every 60s)\n24: cd backend && php bin/console messenger:consume scheduler_default\n25: ```\n26: \n27: **Key URLs:**\n28: - Backend API: `http://localhost:8000/api`\n29: - OpenAPI docs: `http://localhost:8000/api/docs`\n30: - Frontend: `http://localhost:5173`\n31: - Symfony AI docs: https://symfony.com/doc/current/ai/index.html\n32: \n33: ## Project Overview\n34: \n35: **TriageFlow** is a 2-week portfolio project demonstrating AI-assisted patient pre-screening.\n36: \n37: **Core features:**\n38: 1. **Patient Triage Pipeline** — 3-5 step symptom interview → AI analysis → specialist recommendation + urgency + justification\n39: 2. **Admin Panel** — View/export triaged submissions, manage synthetic data generation\n40: 3. **Synthetic Case Generator** — Cron (60s) auto-generates cases via AI so the demo feels alive\n41: \n42: **Constraints:**\n43: - Runs entirely on a laptop (32GB unified memory AMD AI CPU)\n44: - All data is synthetic (no real patient data)\n45: - AI calls use DeepSeek V4 Pro/Flash via `symfony/ai`\n46: - 2-week development window with OpenCode + AI agents\n47: \n48: ## Architecture Decisions\n49: \n50: | Decision | Choice | Rationale |\n51: |----------|--------|-----------|\n52: | Backend Framework | Symfony 7.4 | Market demand (all top offers), `symfony/scheduler` for cron, `symfony/ai` for AI |\n53: | Frontend Framework | React 19 + Vite + TypeScript | Market frequency (15% of Symfony offers), fast HMR for rapid dev |\n54: | AI Integration | `symfony/ai` (v0.9.0) | Official Symfony package, native DeepSeek support, Agent/Chat/Platform components |\n55: | API Layer | API Platform (admin CRUD) + Manual Controllers (triage pipeline) | Shows both productivity and senior-level architecture |\n56: | Architecture Style | DDD Light (Bounded Contexts) | Inspired by CodelyTV/php-ddd-example, sufficient for 2-week scope |\n57: | Async Processing | Symfony Messenger + Scheduler | Handles AI calls asynchronously, cron-based synthetic generation |\n58: | Database | PostgreSQL (primary) | Better JSON support for AI responses, growing market demand (20% of offers) |\n59: | Testing | PHPUnit (backend) + Vitest (frontend) | PHPUnit appears in 45% of senior Symfony offers |\n60: | Containerization | Docker (dev only) | 60% of offers require Docker; TriageFlow uses it for local dev consistency |\n61: \n62: ## Agent & Skill Mapping\n63: \n64: ### OpenCode Agents (invoked via Task tool)\n65: \n66: | Agent | Role | When to Use |\n67: |-------|------|-------------|\n68: | `symfony-specialist` | Symfony 7.x patterns, Doctrine, Messenger, symfony/ai | Backend code, API design, AI integration |\n69: | `frontend-developer` | React + TypeScript components, Vite, Tailwind | Frontend UI, state management, API client |\n70: | `backend-developer` | General backend architecture | Cross-cutting concerns, data modeling |\n71: | `api-designer` | REST API design, JSON:API conventions | API endpoint design, OpenAPI docs |\n72: | `code-reviewer` | Code quality, security, best practices | Before commits, PR review |\n73: | `docker-expert` | Docker Compose, container configuration | Dev environment setup |\n74: | `documentation-engineer` | Technical docs, agents.md, API docs | Documentation updates |\n75: | `test-automator` | Test generation, coverage | Adding test suites |\n76: \n77: ### Skills (loaded via Skill tool)\n78: \n79: ```bash\n80: # Before ANY creative work (features, components, behaviors)\n81: skill(\"brainstorming\")\n82: \n83: # Before writing new features, fixing bugs, refactoring  \n84: skill(\"test-driven-development\")\n85: \n86: # When encountering bugs, test failures, unexpected behavior\n87: skill(\"systematic-debugging\")\n88: \n89: # Before claiming work is complete\n90: skill(\"verification-before-completion\")\n91: \n92: # When receiving code review feedback\n93: skill(\"receiving-code-review\")\n94: ```\n95: \n96: ### Project-Specific Skill\n97: \n98: ```bash\n99: # Load TriageFlow conventions (DDD, AI pipeline, medical domain)\n100: skill(\"triageflow\")\n101: ```\n102: Location: `.opencode/skills/triageflow/SKILL.md`\n103: \n104: ## Development Workflow\n105: \n106: ### Phase 1: Foundation (Days 1-2)\n107: - [x] Infrastructure blueprint (this session)\n108: - [ ] Symfony 7.4 API skeleton with Docker\n109: - [ ] React + Vite + TypeScript frontend skeleton\n110: - [ ] symfony/ai integration with DeepSeek\n111: - [ ] Database schema + Doctrine entities\n112: \n113: ### Phase 2: Core Pipeline (Days 3-4)\n114: - [ ] Patient intake endpoints (symptom questionnaire)\n115: - [ ] AI triage analysis (symfony/ai Agent component)\n116: - [ ] Admin CRUD (API Platform)\n117: - [ ] Triage submission flow end-to-end\n118: \n119: ### Phase 3: Demo Polish (Days 5-6)\n120: - [ ] Synthetic case generator (symfony/scheduler)\n121: - [ ] Admin dashboard with stats\n122: - [ ] Frontend patient interview UI\n123: - [ ] Responsive design + dark mode\n124: \n125: ### Phase 4: Hardening (Days 7-10)\n126: - [ ] Tests (PHPUnit + Vitest, 80%+ coverage)\n127: - [ ] Error handling + retry logic\n128: - [ ] Performance optimization\n129: - [ ] Documentation\n130: \n131: ### Workflow Rules\n132: \n133: 1. **Brainstorm before building** — always invoke `brainstorming` skill before new features\n134: 2. **TDD mandatory** — invoke `test-driven-development` for features/bugfixes\n135: 3. **Single-responsibility commits** — `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `refactor:`\n136: 4. **Verify before claiming done** — invoke `verification-before-completion`\n137: 5. **Code review before merge** — use `code-reviewer` agent\n138: \n139: ## Convention Rules\n140: \n141: ### Always\n142: - [ ] Load `@backend/agents.md` before touching backend code\n143: - [ ] Load `@frontend/agents.md` before touching frontend code\n144: - [ ] Write tests before implementation (TDD)\n145: - [ ] Use strict types (`declare(strict_types=1)`) in PHP\n146: - [ ] Use TypeScript strict mode in frontend\n147: - [ ] All AI calls go through `symfony/ai` Platform component\n148: - [ ] Synthetic data ONLY — never real patient data (even in tests)\n149: \n150: ### Never\n151: - [ ] Skip code review before merging\n152: - [ ] Use `any` in TypeScript\n153: - [ ] Commit secrets or API keys\n154: - [ ] Mix business logic in controllers\n155: - [ ] Skip error handling for AI calls\n156: \n157: ## Directory Structure\n158: \n159: ```\n160: triageflow/\n161: ├── agents.md                    # THIS FILE — master agent configuration\n162: ├── .opencode/\n163: │   ├── config.json              # OpenCode configuration\n164: │   └── skills/\n165: │       └── triageflow/\n166: │           └── SKILL.md         # Project-specific conventions skill\n167: ├── backend/                     # Symfony 7.4 API\n168: │   ├── agents.md                # Backend-specific coding rules\n169: │   ├── config/\n170: │   │   └── packages/\n171: │   │       └── ai.yaml          # symfony/ai DeepSeek configuration\n172: │   ├── src/\n173: │   │   ├── Triage/              # Bounded Context: Triage Pipeline\n174: │   │   │   ├── Application/     # Commands, Queries, Handlers\n175: │   │   │   ├── Domain/          # Entities, Value Objects, Repositories\n176: │   │   │   └── Infrastructure/  # Controllers, API Platform Resources\n177: │   │   ├── Admin/               # Bounded Context: Admin Panel\n178: │   │   └── Reporting/           # Bounded Context: Statistics\n179: │   ├── tests/\n180: │   └── docker-compose.yml\n181: └── frontend/                    # React 19 + Vite + TypeScript\n182:     ├── agents.md                # Frontend-specific coding rules\n183:     ├── src/\n184:     │   ├── components/          # Reusable UI components\n185:     │   ├── features/            # Feature-specific pages/modules\n186:     │   ├── api/                 # API client and types\n187:     │   └── hooks/               # Custom React hooks\n188:     └── tests/\n189: ```\n190: \n191: ## Related Files\n192: \n193: - `backend/agents.md` — Symfony 7.4 backend rules\n194: - `frontend/agents.md` — React frontend rules\n195: - `.opencode/skills/triageflow/SKILL.md` — Domain-specific conventions\n196: - `.opencode/config.json` — OpenCode configuration\n197: - https://github.com/CodelyTV/php-ddd-example — Architecture inspiration\n198: - https://github.com/symfony/ai — Official symfony/ai package\n199: \n200: ## Maintenance\n201: \n202: Update this file when:\n203: - Tech stack changes (new packages, version bumps)\n204: - Architecture decisions evolve\n205: - New bounded contexts are added\n206: - Agent/Skill mappings change\n207: - Workflow rules are refined\n208: \n209: ## Agent skills\n210: \n211: ### Issue tracker\n212: \n213: Issues live as GitHub Issues in `psswid/triageflow-docs`. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n214: \n215: ### Triage labels\n216: \n217: Uses the default five canonical triage labels. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.\n218: \n219: ### Domain docs\n220: \n221: Single-context layout: one `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` at repo root. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.\n\n(End of file - total 221 lines)\n</content>",
