            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/frontend/agents.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TriageFlow Frontend — Agent Configuration\n2: \n3: > React 19 + Vite + TypeScript frontend rules for AI agents. Load this file before ANY frontend work (components, pages, API client, testing). Patient triage interview UI + Admin dashboard.\n4: \n5: ## Quick Reference\n6: \n7: ```bash\n8: # Create React + Vite + TypeScript project\n9: npm create vite@latest frontend -- --template react-ts\n10: \n11: # Install dependencies\n12: npm install react-router-dom @tanstack/react-query\n13: npm install -D tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite vitest @testing-library/react\n14: \n15: # Development\n16: npm run dev            # Start dev server on port 5173\n17: \n18: # Testing\n19: npm run test           # Run Vitest tests\n20: npm run test:watch     # Watch mode\n21: \n22: # Type checking\n23: npm run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit\n24: \n25: # Build\n26: npm run build          # Production build to dist/\n27: ```\n28: \n29: ## Tech Stack\n30: \n31: | Tool | Version | Purpose |\n32: |------|---------|---------|\n33: | React | 19.x | UI framework |\n34: | Vite | 6.x | Build tool + dev server |\n35: | TypeScript | 5.x | Type safety (strict mode) |\n36: | React Router | 7.x | Client-side routing |\n37: | TanStack Query | 5.x | Server state + API caching |\n38: | Tailwind CSS | 4.x | Utility-first styling |\n39: | Vitest | 3.x | Unit/integration testing |\n40: | Testing Library | latest | Component testing |\n41: \n42: ## Directory Structure\n43: \n44: ```\n45: src/\n46: ├── api/\n47: │   ├── client.ts              # Axios/fetch wrapper with JWT\n48: │   ├── endpoints.ts            # API endpoint definitions\n49: │   ├── types.ts                # API response types (generated from OpenAPI)\n50: │   └── hooks.ts                # TanStack Query hooks\n51: ├── components/\n52: │   ├── ui/                     # Reusable UI primitives (Button, Card, Input)\n53: │   │   ├── Button.tsx\n54: │   │   ├── Card.tsx\n55: │   │   └── Input.tsx\n56: │   ├── layout/                 # Layout components\n57: │   │   ├── AppLayout.tsx\n58: │   │   ├── Header.tsx\n59: │   │   └── Sidebar.tsx\n60: │   └── shared/                 # Shared composite components\n61: │       ├── Loader.tsx\n62: │       ├── ErrorBoundary.tsx\n63: │       └── EmptyState.tsx\n64: ├── features/\n65: │   ├── triage/                 # Patient triage interview\n66: │   │   ├── pages/\n67: │   │   │   ├── TriagePage.tsx\n68: │   │   │   └── TriageResultPage.tsx\n69: │   │   ├── components/\n70: │   │   │   ├── SymptomForm.tsx\n71: │   │   │   ├── ProgressBar.tsx\n72: │   │   │   └── ResultCard.tsx\n73: │   │   └── hooks/\n74: │   │       └── useTriage.ts\n75: │   ├── admin/                  # Admin dashboard\n76: │   │   ├── pages/\n77: │   │   │   ├── DashboardPage.tsx\n78: │   │   │   └── SubmissionDetailPage.tsx\n79: │   │   └── components/\n80: │   │       ├── StatsGrid.tsx\n81: │   │       └── SubmissionsTable.tsx\n82: │   └── synthetic/              # Synthetic data status\n83: │       └── components/\n84: │           └── LiveFeed.tsx\n85: ├── hooks/\n86: │   ├── useAuth.ts\n87: │   └── useTheme.ts\n88: ├── lib/\n89: │   ├── utils.ts                # General utilities\n90: │   └── constants.ts            # App constants\n91: ├── styles/\n92: │   ├── index.css               # Tailwind imports + globals\n93: │   └── design-system.css       # Custom design tokens\n94: ├── App.tsx\n95: ├── main.tsx\n96: └── routes.tsx\n97: ```\n98: \n99: ## Component Conventions\n100: \n101: ### Component Pattern\n102: \n103: ```tsx\n104: // ✅ CORRECT: Well-typed functional component\n105: interface SymptomFormProps {\n106:   readonly symptoms: readonly string[];\n107:   readonly onNext: (symptoms: readonly string[]) => void;\n108:   readonly isLoading: boolean;\n109: }\n110: \n111: export function SymptomForm({ symptoms, onNext, isLoading }: SymptomFormProps) {\n112:   const [selected, setSelected] = useState<readonly string[]>([]);\n113: \n114:   const handleToggle = useCallback((symptom: string) => {\n115:     setSelected((prev) =>\n116:       prev.includes(symptom)\n117:         ? prev.filter((s) => s !== symptom)\n118:         : [...prev, symptom],\n119:     );\n120:   }, []);\n121: \n122:   return (\n123:     <div className=\"space-y-4\">\n124:       {symptoms.map((symptom) => (\n125:         <button\n126:           key={symptom}\n127:           onClick={() => handleToggle(symptom)}\n128:           className={clsx(\n129:             'rounded-lg border p-4 transition-colors',\n130:             selected.includes(symptom)\n131:               ? 'border-blue-500 bg-blue-50 dark:border-blue-400 dark:bg-blue-950'\n132:               : 'border-gray-200 hover:border-gray-300 dark:border-gray-700',\n133:           )}\n134:         >\n135:           {symptom}\n136:         </button>\n137:       ))}\n138:       <Button onClick={() => onNext(selected)} disabled={isLoading}>\n139:         {isLoading ? 'Analyzing...' : 'Next'}\n140:       </Button>\n141:     </div>\n142:   );\n143: }\n144: \n145: // ❌ BAD: No types, inline styles, no loading state\n146: export function SymptomForm({ symptoms, onNext }) {\n147:   return <div>{symptoms.map(s => <div onClick={() => onNext([s])}>{s}</div>)}</div>;\n148: }\n149: ```\n150: \n151: ### Rules\n152: - **All components must be functions** — no class components\n153: - **Named exports only** — no default exports for components\n154: - **Props interface co-located** with component\n155: - **`readonly` on all props** — props are never mutated\n156: - **`useCallback` / `useMemo`** for derived values and handlers passed to children\n157: - **Never use `any`** — use `unknown` and type narrowing\n158: - **Error boundaries** at feature level (not per component)\n159: - **Loading states** for every async operation\n160: - **Empty states** for every list component\n161: - **Dark mode** via Tailwind `dark:` variants + system preference detection\n162: \n163: ## State Management\n164: \n165: ### Server State → TanStack Query\n166: \n167: ```tsx\n168: // api/hooks.ts\n169: export function useTriageResult(id: string) {\n170:   return useQuery({\n171:     queryKey: ['triage', id],\n172:     queryFn: () => apiClient.get<TriageResult>(`/api/triage/result/${id}`),\n173:     refetchInterval: (query) => {\n174:       // Poll every 2s while processing\n175:       return query.state.data?.status === 'processing' ? 2000 : false;\n176:     },\n177:   });\n178: }\n179: \n180: export function useSubmitTriage() {\n181:   const queryClient = useQueryClient();\n182: \n183:   return useMutation({\n184:     mutationFn: (data: TriageSubmission) =>\n185:       apiClient.post('/api/triage/submit', data),\n186:     onSuccess: () => {\n187:       queryClient.invalidateQueries({ queryKey: ['submissions'] });\n188:     },\n189:   });\n190: }\n191: ```\n192: \n193: ### Client State → useState / useReducer\n194: \n195: Only for UI-only state (form values, toggles, modals). Everything from the API goes through TanStack Query.\n196: \n197: ## API Client\n198: \n199: ```tsx\n200: // api/client.ts\n201: const apiClient = axios.create({\n202:   baseURL: import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL ?? 'http://localhost:8000',\n203:   headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n204: });\n205: \n206: // JWT interceptor\n207: apiClient.interceptors.request.use((config) => {\n208:   const token = localStorage.getItem('jwt_token');\n209:   if (token) {\n210:     config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;\n211:   }\n212:   return config;\n213: });\n214: \n215: // Error interceptor\n216: apiClient.interceptors.response.use(\n217:   (response) => response,\n218:   (error: AxiosError<ApiErrorResponse>) => {\n219:     if (error.response?.status === 401) {\n220:       localStorage.removeItem('jwt_token');\n221:       window.location.href = '/login';\n222:     }\n223:     return Promise.reject(error);\n224:   },\n225: );\n226: ```\n227: \n228: ### API Rules\n229: - **Single `apiClient` instance** — no scattered fetch calls\n230: - **All API types in `api/types.ts`** — generated from OpenAPI spec when possible\n231: - **TanStack Query for all GET requests** — caching, refetching, polling\n232: - **TanStack Query mutations for POST/PUT/PATCH** — optimistic updates where safe\n233: - **Error handling in interceptor** — not in every component\n234: - **Polling for async endpoints** — triage results use `refetchInterval`\n235: \n236: ## Routing\n237: \n238: ```tsx\n239: // routes.tsx\n240: import { createBrowserRouter } from 'react-router-dom';\n241: \n242: export const router = createBrowserRouter([\n243:   {\n244:     path: '/',\n245:     element: <AppLayout />,\n246:     errorElement: <ErrorBoundary />,\n247:     children: [\n248:       { index: true, element: <HomePage /> },\n249:       { path: 'triage', element: <TriagePage /> },\n250:       { path: 'triage/:id/result', element: <TriageResultPage /> },\n251:       {\n252:         path: 'admin',\n253:         element: <ProtectedRoute />,\n254:         children: [\n255:           { index: true, element: <DashboardPage /> },\n256:           { path: 'submissions/:id', element: <SubmissionDetailPage /> },\n257:         ],\n258:       },\n259:     ],\n260:   },\n261: ]);\n262: ```\n263: \n264: ## Styling with Tailwind CSS\n265: \n266: ### Design Tokens (Tailwind Config)\n267: \n268: ```ts\n269: // tailwind.config.ts\n270: export default {\n271:   darkMode: 'class',\n272:   theme: {\n273:     extend: {\n274:       colors: {\n275:         primary: {\n276:           50: '#eff6ff',\n277:           500: '#3b82f6',\n278:           900: '#1e3a5f',\n279:         },\n280:         urgency: {\n281:           low: '#22c55e',\n282:           medium: '#eab308',\n283:           high: '#f97316',\n284:           emergency: '#ef4444',\n285:         },\n286:       },\n287:     },\n288:   },\n289: };\n290: ```\n291: \n292: ### Rules\n293: - **Tailwind utilities first** — avoid inline styles and CSS modules\n294: - **`clsx` for conditional classes** — never string concatenation\n295: - **Mobile-first** — use `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints\n296: - **Dark mode** — always include `dark:` variants\n297: - **Custom classes** in `design-system.css` for repeated patterns (card, badge, etc.)\n298: - **Accessibility** — WCAG AA minimum (color contrast, focus states, aria labels)\n299: \n300: ## Testing with Vitest\n301: \n302: ```tsx\n303: // SymptomForm.test.tsx\n304: import { render, screen, fireEvent } from '@testing-library/react';\n305: import { SymptomForm } from './SymptomForm';\n306: \n307: describe('SymptomForm', () => {\n308:   const mockSymptoms = ['Chest pain', 'Headache', 'Dizziness'];\n309:   const mockOnNext = vi.fn();\n310: \n311:   it('renders all symptoms as buttons', () => {\n312:     render(\n313:       <SymptomForm\n314:         symptoms={mockSymptoms}\n315:         onNext={mockOnNext}\n316:         isLoading={false}\n317:       />,\n318:     );\n319: \n320:     expect(screen.getByText('Chest pain')).toBeInTheDocument();\n321:     expect(screen.getByText('Headache')).toBeInTheDocument();\n322:     expect(screen.getByText('Dizziness')).toBeInTheDocument();\n323:   });\n324: \n325:   it('toggles symptom selection on click', () => {\n326:     render(\n327:       <SymptomForm\n328:         symptoms={mockSymptoms}\n329:         onNext={mockOnNext}\n330:         isLoading={false}\n331:       />,\n332:     );\n333: \n334:     const chestPain = screen.getByText('Chest pain');\n335:     fireEvent.click(chestPain);\n336:     expect(chestPain).toHaveClass('border-blue-500');\n337: \n338:     fireEvent.click(chestPain);\n339:     expect(chestPain).not.toHaveClass('border-blue-500');\n340:   });\n341: \n342:   it('disables next button when loading', () => {\n343:     render(\n344:       <SymptomForm\n345:         symptoms={mockSymptoms}\n346:         onNext={mockOnNext}\n347:         isLoading={true}\n348:       />,\n349:     );\n350: \n351:     expect(screen.getByText('Analyzing...')).toBeDisabled();\n352:   });\n353: });\n354: ```\n355: \n356: ### Testing Rules\n357: - **Vitest + Testing Library** — no Enzyme, no Jest\n358: - **Test behavior, not implementation** — user interactions, not state internals\n359: - **Mock API calls** via `vi.mock()` or MSW (Mock Service Worker)\n360: - **Test loading, error, and empty states** — not just happy path\n361: - **Accessibility queries** — `getByRole`, `getByLabelText` over `getByTestId`\n362: \n363: ## TypeScript Conventions\n364: \n365: ```tsx\n366: // ✅ Good: Discriminated unions for API states\n367: type TriageState =\n368:   | { status: 'idle' }\n369:   | { status: 'loading' }\n370:   | { status: 'success'; result: TriageResult }\n371:   | { status: 'error'; error: string };\n372: \n373: // ✅ Good: Readonly arrays and objects\n374: interface TriageResult {\n375:   readonly id: string;\n376:   readonly specialist: SpecialistType;\n377:   readonly urgency: UrgencyLevel;\n378:   readonly justification: string;\n379:   readonly submittedAt: string;\n380: }\n381: \n382: // ❌ Bad: any, mutable types\n383: interface BadResult {\n384:   id: any;\n385:   specialist: string;\n386:   urgency: string;\n387: }\n388: ```\n389: \n390: ### Rules\n391: - **Strict mode in `tsconfig.json`** — `strict: true`\n392: - **Interfaces for object shapes** — `type` for unions/primitives\n393: - **`readonly` on all props and return types**\n394: - **Discriminated unions** for loading/error/success states\n395: - **No `as` casts** — use type guards instead\n396: - **`satisfies` operator** for config objects (TypeScript 5.x)\n397: \n398: ## Related Files\n399: \n400: - `../agents.md` — Master project configuration\n401: - `../.opencode/config.json` — OpenCode configuration\n402: - `../.opencode/skills/triageflow/SKILL.md` — Domain conventions\n403: - `../backend/agents.md` — Backend rules (API contracts, response shapes)\n404: \n405: ## Maintenance\n406: \n407: Update this file when:\n408: - New dependencies are added\n409: - Component patterns evolve\n410: - API types change\n411: - New features require new page/component patterns\n412: - Testing strategy changes\n\n(End of file - total 412 lines)\n</content>",
