            "output": "<path>/home/stefan/dev/projects/triageflow/docs/operating-guide.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # TriageFlow — Operating Guide\n2: \n3: > How to run dev sessions efficiently with this agent setup. Read once, keep open as reference.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## What Was Just Set Up\n8: \n9: `/setup-matt-pocock-skills` configured three things agents need:\n10: \n11: | Thing | Where | What it does |\n12: |-------|-------|-------------|\n13: | Issue tracker | GitHub Issues on `triageflow-docs` | `to-issues` creates tickets here. `gh` CLI commands documented in `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md` |\n14: | Triage labels | 5 defaults: `needs-triage`, `needs-info`, `ready-for-agent`, `ready-for-human`, `wontfix` | `triage` skill applies these as issues move through pipeline |\n15: | Domain docs | Single-context: one `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` at root | `grill-with-docs` populates these. Other skills read them to stay in domain language |\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## Starting a Session\n20: \n21: Every session starts from `docs/task-template.md`. Copy it, fill in blanks, paste into OpenCode.\n22: \n23: ```\n24: docs/task-template.md     ← Always start here\n25: ```\n26: \n27: Template has 4 sections:\n28: 1. **Stage** — `starting` / `continuing` / `finishing` (tells agent what phase you're in)\n29: 2. **Context Dependencies** — list files to load before coding (agents.md, backend/agents.md, frontend/agents.md, CONTEXT.md)\n30: 3. **Pipeline** — checkboxes for gates: align → plan → issues → implement → test → review → verify → handoff\n31: 4. **Problem/Context** — what you're trying to do\n32: \n33: ---\n34: \n35: ## Which Docs to Read When\n36: \n37: Three scenario files — read the right one for your situation:\n38: \n39: | Situation | Read this |\n40: |-----------|-----------|\n41: | Starting ANY coding session | `docs/task-template.md` (fill and paste) |\n42: | \"What tools do I use to do X?\" (process question) | `docs/tools-scenarios-matrix.md` — 11 process scenarios |\n43: | Backend coding (Symfony, Doctrine, symfony/ai) | `docs/tools-scenarios-backend.md` — 13 Symfony scenarios |\n44: | Frontend coding (React, Vite, TanStack, Tailwind) | `docs/tools-scenarios-frontend.md` — 13 React scenarios |\n45: | Domain language / architecture decisions | `CONTEXT.md` + `docs/adr/` (created by `grill-with-docs`) |\n46: | Agent rules + conventions | `agents.md` (root) → then `backend/agents.md` or `frontend/agents.md` |\n47: \n48: Flow:\n49: ```\n50: Start session → task-template.md → pick scenario file → follow gate pipeline → handoff at end\n51: ```\n52: \n53: ---\n54: \n55: ## Key Skills — When to Invoke\n56: \n57: Six most common. Others in the scenario files.\n58: \n59: | Skill | Invocation | When |\n60: |-------|-----------|------|\n61: | Grill with docs | `skill(\"grill-with-docs\")` | Start of ANY new feature or architecture change. Defines language, creates ADRs. Never skip |\n62: | Write plan + TaskManager | `skill(\"writing-plans\")` → `task(subagent=\"TaskManager\")` | Feature touches 4+ files. Breaks into parallel/sequential subtasks |\n63: | To issues | `skill(\"to-issues\")` | After plan is written. Converts plan → GitHub issues |\n64: | TDD workflow | `skill(\"tdd-workflow\")` | Writing ANY code. Red → green → refactor. Don't skip for \"simple\" changes |\n65: | Request review | `skill(\"requesting-code-review\")` | After implementation. Gets CodeReviewer to check conventions, security, patterns |\n66: | Verify | `skill(\"verification-before-completion\")` | Before claiming \"done.\" Runs tests, lint, checks. Evidence before assertions |\n67: | Handoff | `skill(\"handoff\")` | End of EVERY session. Creates committable .md. Your continuity when DCP compresses old content |\n68: \n69: On-demand:\n70: - `skill(\"zoom-out\")` — agent tunnel-visioning, missing big picture\n71: - `skill(\"caveman\")` — session bloated (100+ messages), cut tokens 75%\n72: - `skill(\"systematic-debugging\")` — bug hunting, root cause analysis\n73: \n74: ---\n75: \n76: ## The Core Pipeline (Repeated Every Session)\n77: \n78: ```\n79: 1. 🧠 ALIGN    → grill-with-docs (domain language + ADRs)\n80: 2. 📋 PLAN     → writing-plans → TaskManager (subtask breakdown)\n81: 3. 🎫 ISSUES   → to-issues (plan → GitHub tickets)\n82: 4. 🔨 BUILD    → tdd-workflow → CoderAgent (execute subtasks)\n83: 5. 🧪 TEST     → TestEngineer (fill coverage gaps)\n84: 6. 👁️ REVIEW   → CodeReviewer (quality + security check)\n85: 7. ✅ VERIFY   → verification-before-completion (tests pass, lint clean)\n86: 8. 📦 HANDOFF  → handoff (session summary → .md)\n87: ```\n88: \n89: Shortcut for quick bugs: `systematic-debugging → zoom-out → tdd → review → verify` (skip plan/issues if <3 files)\n90: \n91: ---\n92: \n93: ## Repo Layout — Three Repos, One Project\n94: \n95: | Repo | GitHub | Contains |\n96: |------|--------|----------|\n97: | `triageflow-docs` | `psswid/triageflow-docs` | OpenCode config, docs, agents.md, raw_log.md. Issues live here |\n98: | `triageflow-backend` | `psswid/triageflow-backend` | Symfony 7.4 backend, separate git history |\n99: | `triageflow-frontend` | `psswid/triageflow-frontend` | React 19 frontend, separate git history |\n100: \n101: **How to work across repos:**\n102: - Issues → always in `triageflow-docs`\n103: - Backend code → work in `triageflow/backend/` (has its own `.git/`)\n104: - Frontend code → work in `triageflow/frontend/` (has its own `.git/`)\n105: - Docs/config → work in `triageflow/` root (docs-repo)\n106: - Session handoffs → committed to docs-repo\n107: \n108: ---\n109: \n110: ## Quick Reference — Common Terminal Commands\n111: \n112: ```bash\n113: # Docs repo\n114: git status                    # Check what changed in docs/config\n115: git push                      # Push docs/config changes\n116: \n117: # Backend (cd backend first)\n118: php bin/phpunit               # Run backend tests\n119: php bin/console make:entity   # Generate entity\n120: php bin/console make:migration # Generate migration\n121: symfony server:start          # Start dev server\n122: \n123: # Frontend (cd frontend first)\n124: npm run dev                   # Start Vite dev server\n125: npm run test                  # Run Vitest tests\n126: npm run build                 # Production build\n127: npx tsc --noEmit              # TypeScript check\n128: ```\n129: \n130: ---\n131: \n132: ## First-Time Setup (Do Once)\n133: \n134: Already done if you just ran `/setup-matt-pocock-skills`:\n135: \n136: ```bash\n137: # 1. Install Matt Pocock skills\n138: npx skills@latest add mattpocock/skills\n139: # → Select: setup-matt-pocock-skills, grill-with-docs, handoff, to-issues, zoom-out, caveman\n140: \n141: # 2. Run setup (creates docs/agents/*.md + updates agents.md)\n142: # → Already done\n143: \n144: # 3. Create GitHub labels (after first gh auth)\n145: gh label create \"needs-triage\" --color \"d73a4a\" --repo psswid/triageflow-docs\n146: gh label create \"needs-info\" --color \"0075ca\" --repo psswid/triageflow-docs\n147: gh label create \"ready-for-agent\" --color \"0e8a16\" --repo psswid/triageflow-docs\n148: gh label create \"ready-for-human\" --color \"fbca04\" --repo psswid/triageflow-docs\n149: gh label create \"wontfix\" --color \"ffffff\" --repo psswid/triageflow-docs\n150: ```\n\n(End of file - total 150 lines)\n</content>",
