, ORTHOPEDIST, GASTROENTEROLOGIST, PULMONOLOGIST, PSYCHIATRIST\n- Synthetic Case: An AI-generated fake patient case for demo purposes\n- Triage Pipeline: The 3-5 step symptom interview → AI analysis → result\n- Admin Panel: View/export submissions, manage synthetic data\n- Scheduler: Cron-based synthetic case generation (every 60s)\n\nBut there are fuzzy areas I should grill the user about:\n\n1. **\"Triage Pipeline\" vs \"Triage Flow\" vs \"Patient Intake\"** — these terms are used interchangeably in the docs. What's the canonical term? Is \"triage\" the entire process, and \"intake\" is the symptom-gathering step?\n\n2. **\"Patient\" vs \"User\" vs \"Submitter\"** — The docs mention \"patient\" but TriageFlow is a demo with synthetic data. Is the person submitting symptoms a \"patient\"? If admin staff are submitting on behalf of patients, are they still called \"patients\"?\n\n3. **\"Admin\" vs \"Administrator\" vs \"Reviewer\"** — Who uses the admin panel? Is it a medical professional reviewing triage results, or a system administrator managing the application?\n\n4. **Relationship between TriageSubmission and TriageResult** — Is this 1:1? Does every submission always get a result? What about submissions that fail AI processing?\n\n5. **\"Synthetic Case Generator\" vs \"Synthetic Data\"** — Is a \"synthetic case\" the same as a synthetic TriageSubmission? \n\n6. **The interview flow** — The docs say \"3-5 step symptom interview.\" What are the steps exactly? Is it a wizard-style multi-page form or a single-page form?\n\n7. **\"Processing\" vs \"Analyzing\"** — The entity has statuses (pending, processing, completed, failed). Are these the canonical statuses? Is there a distinction between \"processing\" (in queue) and \"analyzing\" (AI is running)?\n\n8. **About the term \"Triage\" itself** — In medical context, triage is about prioritizing patients by severity. In TriageFlow, is it about recommending specialists? Or both?\n\nLet me start the grilling. One question at a time, with recommended answers.\n\nLet me start with the most fundamental question: the core domain concept.",
