          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Good. Now next question. The Triage Submission lifecycle.\n\nThe backend/agents.md defines an entity with:\n- status: pending, processing, completed, failed\n- submittedAt, processedAt\n- isSynthetic flag\n\nThe API design says:\n- POST /api/triage/submit → 202 Accepted (async)\n- GET /api/triage/status/{id} → check processing status\n- GET /api/triage/result/{id} → get AI triage result\n\nSo the flow is:\n1. User submits → Triage Submission created with status \"pending\"\n2. Messenger picks it up → status changes to \"processing\"\n3. AI analysis runs → status changes to \"completed\" or \"failed\"\n4. User can poll for status, then get result when completed\n\nBut I'm not clear on:\n- Is TriageResult a separate entity from TriageSubmission? The backend doc shows them as separate entities.\n- The \"3-5 step symptom interview\" - is this a multi-step wizard form, or a single form with multiple sections?\n\nLet me ask about the submission lifecycle and the interview flow.\n\nActually, let me ask about both at once since they're related.",
