          "text": "Good. Now let me move on to the Admin side. The agents.md mentions:\n- Admin panel: View/export triaged submissions, manage synthetic data generation\n- Admin dashboard with stats\n- API Platform for admin CRUD\n- Synthetic case generator (cron every 60s)\n\nBut I need to nail down the Admin side more precisely. Key questions:\n\n1. What exactly is the Admin dashboard showing? A live feed of submissions? Stats? Both?\n2. Is the synthetic case generator running continuously, or does the Admin trigger it?\n3. What kind of stats? \n4. Does the Admin have any actions beyond viewing? (Export? Override triage? Delete?)\n\nLet me think about what I'd recommend...\n\nThe agents.md already has some answers:\n- `GET /api/admin/stats` — Dashboard statistics\n- `POST /api/admin/synthetic/generate` — Manually trigger synthetic case\n- `PATCH /api/admin/submissions/{id}` — Update status/override\n- Scheduler runs auto every 60s\n\nSo there IS manual trigger AND automatic cron.\n\nLet me ask about:\n1. The admin dashboard contents (what stats, what live view)\n2. The synthetic case generation flow (auto vs manual)\n3. Admin actions on submissions",
