        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 5: The Admin experience — what exactly happens on the dashboard?**\n\nThe agents.md describes the admin as monitoring a \"live simulation.\" I want to pin down what they actually see and do. Three things need resolution:\n\n**5a. What's on the dashboard?**\n\nThe agents.md mentions \"Dashboard statistics\" but doesn't specify what stats. Possibilities:\n- Total submissions, by status (pending/processing/completed/failed)\n- Submissions over time (line chart)\n- Specialist/urgency distribution (pie/bar charts)\n- Average processing time\n- Synthetic vs. user-submitted ratio\n\n**My recommendation:** Keep it portfolio-relevant. A stats row (total, completed today, avg processing time) + a live-feed table of recent submissions with status badges + specialist/urgency distribution. Enough to show you can build real-time dashboards, not a full analytics suite.\n\n**5b. Synthetic case generation — auto, manual, or both?**\n\nThe docs show both a scheduler (auto every 60s) AND a manual trigger endpoint (`POST /api/admin/synthetic/generate`). \n\n**My recommendation:** Both. The scheduler runs in the background to keep the demo \"alive\" (new submissions appearing without intervention). The manual trigger lets an Admin demonstrate \"look, I can generate a case right now\" during a portfolio walkthrough. Both flow through the same pipeline.\n\n**5c. What can an Admin DO to a submission?**\n\nThe API lists `PATCH /api/admin/submissions/{id}` for \"Update status/override.\" Does the Admin override AI results? Mark as reviewed? Delete?\n\n**My recommendation:** View-only for the demo. The Admin can see all submissions, filter by status/specialist/urgency, and view full conversation history. Maybe an \"export\" action. But overriding AI results adds complexity without portfolio value — the AI IS the feature being demonstrated.\n\n**Agree/disagree on these three?**\n\n\n\n",
