          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 6: Synthetic Cases — what exactly gets generated?**\n\nThe agents.md shows a `GenerateSyntheticCaseTask` that asks the AI to \"generate 1 realistic but synthetic patient symptom set as JSON array of strings.\" The entity has an `isSynthetic` flag.\n\nBut I need to know: what's the full artifact created?\n\n| Option | What the generator creates |\n|--------|--------------------------|\n| **A: Just the initial symptom description** | AI generates \"chest pain, shortness of breath, dizziness\" → the rest (follow-up Q&A, final result) flows through the same pipeline as a user-submitted case |\n| **B: A complete past submission** | AI generates the entire conversation history + result in one shot, inserted directly into the DB as completed |\n\n**My recommendation: Option A.** The generator creates just the Initial Symptom Description and submits it to the pipeline. The AI-driven interview and triage analysis run exactly as they do for a real User. This keeps the demo honest — the live feed shows the full processing flow (pending → processing → completed), and the Admin sees the pipeline working end-to-end. Option B would skip the most interesting part of the demo.\n\nA **Synthetic Case** is then: a Triage Submission where `isSynthetic = true` and the Initial Symptom Description was generated by the scheduler/manual-trigger rather than a User.\n\n**Agree?**\n\n\n\n",
