          "text": "OK so the user is clear:\n- DeepSeek is for development (the agent coding, the AI that helps build the app)\n- OpenRouter free models are for the app itself (the triage pipeline, synthetic case generation)\n- They're not paying for demo traffic\n\nThis makes sense - DeepSeek is the LLM powering OpenCode/Cursor/Claude Code for development, and OpenRouter free models are used by the running application for triage analysis.\n\nThis is a significant architecture decision that changes what's in agents.md (backend/agents.md says DeepSeek for symfony/ai config). This IS ADR-worthy:\n1. Hard to reverse? Medium - changes symfony/ai platform configuration\n2. Surprising without context? Yes - readers would expect DeepSeek based on the existing docs\n3. Result of a real trade-off? Yes - free vs paid, quality vs cost\n\nSo I'll need to create an ADR for this. But the skill says to offer ADRs sparingly - and this one meets all three criteria.\n\nBut wait, the user also said \"we are using deepseek for development\" - meaning DeepSeek is the coding LLM, not the app's AI. So maybe the confusion was just about terminology. The app uses OpenRouter free models, the development process uses DeepSeek.\n\nLet me not create an ADR for this right now. The CONTEXT.md is about domain language, not infrastructure decisions. The agents.md can be updated later. For now, let me ask the remaining domain questions.\n\nWhat else is left to grill about?\n\nDomain concepts still to pin down:\n- What does the User see after submission? A single result page or a submission history dashboard?\n- The conversation storage format\n- Any other terms?\n\nI think the next most important thing is the User's post-submission experience. Let me ask that.",
