        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "That's clear — app runs on free OpenRouter models, development runs on DeepSeek. Makes sense for a demo. (That's an ADR-worthy decision — noted for later, but let's finish domain language first.)\n\n---\n\n**Question 8: The User's experience — what do they see after submitting?**\n\nYou've described the interview flow (initial description → AI follow-ups → result). But I want to nail down what the User sees when the interview is done, and what they see if they come back later.\n\n**8a. Single result view, or submission history?**\n\n| Option | UX |\n|--------|-----|\n| **A: Single flow** | Submit → wait → see result. No history. Each visit is a fresh submission. |\n| **B: Result page + history** | Submit → result page with their submission. A \"My Submissions\" page lists all their past submissions with statuses. |\n\n**My recommendation: Option B.** For a portfolio project, a \"My Submissions\" page shows database relationships, list views, status badges, and TanStack Query patterns. A single-flow app would be too thin to demonstrate real skills. Plus, Users log in — there should be something to see when they return.\n\n**8b. What's on the result page?**\n\nAfter the AI produces a result, what does the User see? The specialist recommendation + urgency + justification? The full conversation history? Just the conclusion?\n\n**My recommendation:** Full result card showing: recommended specialist (with icon/badge), urgency level (color-coded), medical justification text, and the full conversation history below (collapsible). This lets a portfolio reviewer see both the AI output quality AND the interview flow in one view.\n\n**Agree?**",
