        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 9: Edge cases — what happens when things go wrong?**\n\nTwo things to pin down:\n\n**9a. AI failure — what does the User see?**\n\nIf the AI call fails (timeout, bad response, rate limit on the free OpenRouter tier), the Triage Submission goes to `status: failed`. What happens from the User's perspective?\n\n| Option | UX |\n|--------|-----|\n| **A: Silent failure** | \"Something went wrong. Please try again.\" Generic error, no retry. |\n| **B: Retry + transparency** | \"AI analysis failed. Retrying automatically...\" (backend retries up to 3x via Messenger). If all retries fail, show \"Analysis unavailable — please try again later.\" |\n| **C: Graceful degradation** | Force a result from whatever data was gathered. Mark as \"limited analysis.\" |\n\n**My recommendation: Option B.** Messenger retry strategy is already in the agents.md, and showing the retry UX demonstrates error handling patterns. Failed submissions stay in history with a \"failed\" badge so the User can retry manually if they want.\n\n**9b. Specialist types and urgency levels — are these final?**\n\nThe agents.md lists these enum values. Any changes?\n\n```\nSpecialistType: GP, CARDIOLOGIST, DERMATOLOGIST, NEUROLOGIST, \n                ORTHOPEDIST, GASTROENTEROLOGIST, PULMONOLOGIST, PSYCHIATRIST\nUrgencyLevel:   LOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, EMERGENCY\n```\n\n\n\n",
