          "text": "---\n\n**Question 11: Authentication & registration**\n\nThe agents.md specifies JWT via `lexik/jwt-authentication-bundle`. Two things to nail down:\n\n**11a. Registration — open or admin-gated?**\n\n| Option | Flow |\n|--------|------|\n| **A: Open registration** | Anyone can sign up. Registration page is public. |\n| **B: Admin-invite-only** | Only Admins can create User accounts. No public sign-up. |\n\n**My recommendation: Option A.** It's a demo app — let people self-register and try the triage interview. Admins are a separate concern (seeded account, or separate registration path).\n\n**11b. Single JWT with roles, or separate tokens?**\n\nBoth User and Admin authenticate with JWT. Same token with role claims (`ROLE_USER`, `ROLE_ADMIN`), or different auth endpoints?\n\n**My recommendation:** Single JWT with role claims. One login endpoint, one token that carries roles. Admin routes check for `ROLE_ADMIN`. Simple, and it lets us add roles later (like the \"medic/specialist\" role you mentioned for future expansion).\n\n**Agree?**\n\n\n\n",
