        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\n**Question 12: Frontend-backend communication for the interview**\n\nThe interview is conversational — User sends initial description, AI responds with a question, User answers, etc. Since AI calls are async (via Messenger), the frontend needs to handle the \"waiting for AI\" state.\n\n| Pattern | How it works |\n|---------|-------------|\n| **A: Polling** | POST → get submission ID → poll `GET /status/{id}` every 2s → when status=completed, fetch result. Simple, reliable. |\n| **B: Server-Sent Events (SSE)** | POST → open SSE stream → backend pushes AI responses as they arrive. Real-time, but more complex. |\n\n**My recommendation: Option A.** Polling is simpler to implement, works everywhere, and the agents.md already has TanStack Query polling patterns (`refetchInterval`). The ~2-3s delay between AI responses is fine for a demo — real-time SSE doesn't add portfolio value proportional to its complexity, and the 10s cooldown on synthetic cases makes it moot anyway.\n\n**Agree?**\n\n\n\n",
