        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "---\n\nI think we've covered the domain language thoroughly. Before moving to ADRs, let me check: one decision meets all three ADR criteria.\n\n**AI Provider choice (OpenRouter free → ADR 0001)**\n\nIt's hard to reverse (API integration), surprising (agents.md says DeepSeek), and a real trade-off (cost-free vs. quality). I recommend creating `docs/adr/0001-openrouter-free-models.md`.\n\nBefore I write it — one more check. I've been asking about the system's happy path. Let me do a concrete scenario to stress-test the domain model:\n\n---\n\n**Scenario stress-test:**\n\n*\"A User named Alice registers. She describes 'really bad stomach pain after eating, bloating, diarrhea for 3 days.' The AI asks about blood in stool. Alice says no. AI produces result: GASTROENTEROLOGIST, HIGH urgency. She views the result and logs out. Later she logs back in and visits My Submissions — she sees her past submission.\"*\n\nTwo questions this raises:\n\n1. **What's the \"result\" within a Triage Submission?** The entity has `specialist`, `urgency`, `justification` as direct fields. But it also has the full conversation history. Are those fields the \"result\"? Or is the result a section within the entity that includes those + a summary? We said \"no separate TriageResult entity\" — just confirming those fields live directly on TriageSubmission.\n\n2. **Notification/polling: how does Alice know the interview moved to the next Turn?** She submits her answer, then the frontend polls. When the AI response comes back, the frontend shows the next AI question (or the final result). Does the Triage Submission have a \"current Turn number\" field tracking progress?\n\nLet me not over-complicate this — the entity status + conversation array are sufficient. Let me just verify there are no hidden gaps.\n\nActually, I think we're done with the domain model. Let me propose the ADR and see if the user wants to proceed to the plan stage.---\n\n**Question 13 (final domain check): What fields constitute the AI \"result\"?**\n\nWhen the AI produces its final answer (specialist, urgency, justification) — where does it live in the entity?\n\n| Option | Model |\n|--------|-------|\n| **A: Direct entity fields** | `specialist` (enum), `urgency` (enum), `justification` (text) as columns on TriageSubmission, populated on completion |\n| **B: JSON blob in conversation** | The result is just the last Turn in the conversation history JSON array |\n\n**My recommendation: Option A.** Direct columns are queryable (Admin dashboard: \"show me all HIGH urgency submissions\"), type-safe in Doctrine, and simpler for API responses. The conversation history is the raw transcript; the result fields are the structured extraction.\n\n**That correct?**\n\n\n\n",
