              "command": "gh issue create \\\n  --repo psswid/triageflow-docs \\\n  --title \"3. Triage Interview: AI-driven chat with polling\" \\\n  --label \"ready-for-agent\" \\\n  --body '## What to build\n\nThe core feature: User describes symptoms in free text → AI (OpenRouter via symfony/ai) conducts follow-up interview (max 3 turns) → produces triage result (specialist, urgency, justification). Async via Messenger. React chat UI with polling. Result page with specialist card + conversation history. My Submissions history page.\n\n**Before starting — fetch current docs:**\n- `context7 symfony/ai` — PlatformInterface, Request/Response models, OpenRouter provider config, Agent setup\n- `context7 symfony messenger` — doctrine://default transport, AsMessageHandler, retry_strategy, routing\n- `context7 symfony validator` — Assert\\Collection constraints for triage DTOs\n- `context7 doctrine` — JSON column type, enumType mapping, uuid_generator, ServiceEntityRepository\n- `context7 tanstack` — useMutation, useQuery with refetchInterval polling, query invalidation\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `POST /api/triage/submit` accepts { initialDescription } → returns 202 with submission ID\n- [ ] Messenger transport processes AI calls asynchronously (doctrine://default)\n- [ ] AI receives full conversation history each turn and responds with either {\"type\":\"question\"} or {\"type\":\"result\"}\n- [ ] Interview caps at 3 turns — backend forces final result if AI hasn not produced one\n- [ ] `GET /api/triage/status/{id}` returns current status + last AI message for polling\n- [ ] `POST /api/triage/{id}/answer` adds user answer and dispatches next AI turn\n- [ ] `GET /api/triage/result/{id}` returns full TriageSubmission with conversation history\n- [ ] Chat UI: initial symptom textarea → AI \"typing\" indicator → AI question → user answer input → repeat\n- [ ] Polling every 2s while status is pending/processing\n- [ ] Result page: specialist card (icon + name), urgency badge (color-coded), justification text, collapsible conversation history\n- [ ] My Submissions page: list with status badges, urgency badges, timestamps, click to view result\n- [ ] Failed submissions show error state with retry option\n\n## Tech stack\n\nsymfony/ai-bundle (OpenRouter: google/gemma-4-31b-it:free), Symfony Messenger, Doctrine JSON columns, PHP 8.4 enums, React 19, TanStack Query 5, React Router 7\n\n## Implementation plans\n\n- Backend: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-28-backend-foundation.md` Tasks 4, 6, 9, 10, 11, 12\n- Frontend: `docs/superpowers/plans/2026-05-28-frontend-foundation.md` Tasks 4, 5, 6\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- #2 User Authentication' 2>&1"
